* Fender '65 Deluxe Reverb reissue vibrato (optical tremolo), drawing 041285 rev B: V5A is a three-section RC
* phase-shift oscillator (speed pot in the first section), V5B a pulse driver whose plate current lights the LED
* of the optocoupler OP1 through R47. The photocell side (OP1 pins 3/4) is part of preamp.net: it shunts the
* mixing node through the Intensity pot, and the engine sets its resistance from the LED current. This circuit is
* solved at a low rate of its own (see "vibrato" in amp.json). Same circuit as the Twin's with the Deluxe's values.
*
* The footswitch / Vibrato-off state is the bias reference node t31: about -7 V (V5A cut off) when off (the
* drawing says -6.8 V at TP26), about -0.2 V when the footswitch brings it to ground through R36 10k.

V VRAIL x 100 330

* V5A oscillator: 220k plate load, 2.7k / 22u cathode, the three-section network (.022u, .01u, .01u) with the 100k
* and the 3M speed pot in the first section and 1M to the bias reference in the others.
R R43 x p5a 220k
T V5A n3 p5a k5a 12AX7
R R44 k5a 0 2k7
C C23 k5a 0 22u
C C22 p5a n1 22n
C C21 n1 n2 10n
C C20 n2 n3 10n
R R41 n1 ns 100k
R R_SPEED ns 0 1.5M
R R39 n2 t31 1M
R R40 n3 t31 1M

* Bias reference: -49 V (TP5) through 2.2M against 390k to ground and 4.7u; the footswitch shorts it to ground.
V VBIAS bs 1k -49
R R38 bs t31 2M2
R R37 t31 0 390k
C C19 t31 0 4.7u
R SW_VIB t31 0 1e12

* V5B driver and the LED: 100k from the rail, the LED (pins 2 -> 1) in series with the plate, 10M across.
T V5B n2 p5b k5b 12AX7
R R46 k5b 0 100k
C C24 k5b 0 22u
R R47 x ln 100k
D LED ln p5b SIGNAL
R R45 ln p5b 10M
C C40 p5b 0 22n
